          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#statement"} Statement
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PatchesOfOpenCoverOfNormalSpaceMayBeMadeSmallerSoThatTheirClosuresAreContained"}
            below) states that on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal topological space
            the patches of every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite cover
            may be replaced by smaller patches which still cover the space, but such that their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closures"} topological closures
            are contained in the original patches.
          %p
            If there is more than a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable set
            of elements in the original cover, then this conclusion requires
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zorn%27s+lemma"} Zorn's lemma
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
          %p
            The shrinking lemma is needed in the proof that
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+Hausdorff+spaces+equivalently+admit+subordinate+partitions+of+unity"} paracompact Hausdorff spaces equivalently admit subordinate partitions of unity
          %h2#statement Statement
          #PatchesOfOpenCoverOfNormalSpaceMayBeMadeSmallerSoThatTheirClosuresAreContained.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %strong (shrinking lemma for locally finite covers)
            %p
              Assuming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              then:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            %p
              Then there exists another open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_i)
              of its elements is contained in the original patches:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{i \in I}{\forall}
                    \\left(
                    V_i \subset Cl(V_i) \subset U_i
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
          %p
            We now
            %strong prove
            this in increasing generality, first for binary open covers (lemma
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkingLemmaForBinaryCover"}
            below), then for finite covers (lemma
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkinglemmaForFiniteCovers"}
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkingLemmaForLocallyFiniteCountableCovers"}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PatchesOfOpenCoverOfNormalSpaceMayBeMadeSmallerSoThatTheirClosuresAreContained"}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#PatchesOfOpenCoverOfNormalSpaceMayBeMadeSmallerSoThatTheirClosuresAreContained"} below
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
          #ShrinkingLemmaForBinaryCover.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              %strong (shrinking lemma for binary covers)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal topological space
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in \{1,2\}}
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              by two
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
            %p
              Then there exists an open set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \subset X
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              is contained in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_1 \subset Cl(V_1) \subset U_1
            %p
              and such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_1,U_2\}
              is still an open cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∪
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \cup U_2 = X
              it follows (by
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Morgan%27s+law"} de Morgan's law
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complements"} complements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \backslash U_i
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+subset"} disjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subsets"} closed subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              there exist disjoint open subsets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_1 \supset X \backslash U_2
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    V_2 \supset X \backslash U_1
                    \\,.
            %p By their disjointness, we have the following inclusions:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    V_1 \subset X \backslash V_2 \subset U_1
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \backslash V_2
              is closed, this means that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                      %mo \
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_1) \subset X \backslash V_2
            %p
              Hence it only remains to observe that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∪
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \cup U_2 = X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1
          #ShrinkinglemmaForFiniteCovers.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_3 Lemma
            %p
              %strong (shrinking lemma for finite covers)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in \{1, \cdots, n\}}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              of patches. Then there exists another open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V_i) \subset U_i
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
              using lemma
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkingLemmaForBinaryCover"}
            %p
              To begin with, consider
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %munderover
                        %mo ∪
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ U_1, \underoverset{i = 2}{n}{\cup} U_i\}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkingLemmaForBinaryCover"}
              gives an open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \subset X
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_1 \subset Cl(V_1) \subset U_1
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %munderover
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_1, \underoverset{i = 2}{n}{\cup} U_i\}
              is still an open cover, and accordingly so is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∪
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{ V_1  \} \cup \left\{ U_i \right\}_{i \in \{2, \cdots, n\}}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Similarly we next find an open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_2 \subset X
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_2 \subset Cl(V_2) \subset U_2
              and such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∪
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 3
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{ V_1, ,V_2  \} \cup \left\{ U_i \right\}_{i \in \{3, \cdots, n\}}
            %p
              is an open cover. After
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              such steps we are left with an open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in \{1, \cdots, n\}}
              as required.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Beware that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
              in lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkinglemmaForFiniteCovers"}
              does
              %em not
              give the statement for infinite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+covers"} countable covers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i \in \mathbb{N}}{\cup} V_i
              is a cover.
            %p
              And in fact, assuming the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dowker+space"} Dowker space
              due to
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Beslagic85"} Beslagic 85
          %p
            This issue is evaded if we consider
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+covers"} locally finite covers
          #ShrinkingLemmaForLocallyFiniteCountableCovers.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_4 Lemma
            %p
              %strong (shrinking lemma for locally finite countable covers)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+topological+space"} normal topological space
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in \mathbb{N}}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+cover"} countable cover
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i \subset X
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathbb{N}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i \subset Cl(V_i) \subset U_i
              and such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in \mathbb{N}}
              is still a cover.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              As in the proof of lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkinglemmaForFiniteCovers"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \mathbb{N}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i \subset Cl(V_i) \subset U_i
              and such that for every finite number, hence every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munderover
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∪
                    %munderover
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underoverset{i = 0}{n}{\cup} V_i \cup
                    \\underoverset{i = n+1}{\infty}{\cup} U_i
                    \\;=\; X\,.
            %p
              Now the extra assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finite+cover"} locally finite
              implies that every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              is contained in only finitely many of the
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              there exists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n_x \in \mathbb{N}
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∉
                    %munderover
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi x
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x \notin \underoverset{i = n_x+1}{\infty}{\cup} U_i
                    \\,.
            %p
              This implies that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %munderover
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    x \in \underoverset{i = 0}{n_x}{\cup} V_i
                    \\subset \underset{i \in \mathbb{N}}{\cup} V_i
            %p
              hence that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in \mathbb{N}}
              is indeed a cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            We now invoke
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zorn%27s+lemma"} Zorn's lemma
            to generalize the shrinking lemma for finitely many patches (lemma
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkinglemmaForFiniteCovers"}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              of the general shrinking lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PatchesOfOpenCoverOfNormalSpaceMayBeMadeSmallerSoThatTheirClosuresAreContained"}
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              be the given locally finite cover of the normal space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi τ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\tau)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J, \mathcal{V})
              consisting of
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset I
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  = succeed "-indexed" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒱
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V} = \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
            %p with the property that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Cl
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i \in J \subset I) \Rightarrow ( Cl(V_i) \subset U_i )
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                        %mo \
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i \in I \backslash J) \Rightarrow ( V_i = U_i )
                  \.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mi i
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{V_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
                  is an open cover of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              Equip the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+order"} partial order
              by setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒱
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒲
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mn 2
                        %mo )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mtext and
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %munder
                          %mo ∀
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %msub
                              %mi J
                              %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mi i
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi W
                            %mi i
                          %mo )
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    (J_1, \mathcal{V})
                    \\leq
                    (J_2, \mathcal{W})
                    \\right)
                    \\Leftrightarrow
                    \\left(
                    \\left(
                    J_1 \subset J_2
                    \\right)
                    \\,\text{and}\,
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{i \in J_1}{\forall}
                    \\left(
                    V_i = W_i
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              By definition, an element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = I
              is an open cover of the required form.
            %p
              We claim now that a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+element"} maximal element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J, \mathcal{V})
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\leq)
              has
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                      %mo =
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = I
            %p
              For assume on the contrary that there were
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                      %mo \
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I \backslash J
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ShrinkingLemmaForBinaryCover"}
              to replace that single
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i
              with a smaller open subset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'_i
              to obtain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}'
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cl(V'_i) \subset V_i
              and such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}'
              is still an open cover. But that would mean that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒱
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo ∪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒱
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J,\mathcal{V}) \lt (J \cup \{i\}, \mathcal{V}')
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J,\mathcal{V})
              is maximal. This
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+by+contradiction"} proves by contradiction
              that a maximal element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\leq)
              has
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = I
              and hence is an open cover as required.
            %p
              We are reduced now to showing that a maximal element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\leq)
              exists. To achieve this we invoke
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zorn%27s+lemma"} Zorn's lemma
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain"} chain
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\leq)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} totally ordered
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              has an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+bound"} upper bound
            %p
              So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \subset S
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+order"} totally ordered
              subset. Consider the union of all the index sets appearing in the pairs in this subset:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi J
                        %mo ,
                        %mi 𝒱
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi T
                    %mi J
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\underset{(J,\mathcal{V}) \in T  }{\cup} J
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now define open subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_i
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in K
              picking any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J,\mathcal{V})
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in J
              and setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi i
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W_i \coloneqq V_i \phantom{AAA} i \in K
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is independent of the choice of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo ,
                      %mi 𝒱
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J,\mathcal{V})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,\leq)
              is totally ordered.
            %p
              Moreover, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                    %mo \
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I\backslash K
              define
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                    %mo \
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W_i \coloneqq U_i  \phantom{AAA} i \in I \backslash K
                    \\,.
            %p
              We claim now that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{W_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              thus defined is a cover of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U_i
              for some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \notin K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i = W_i
              and therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo ∪
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i \in I}{\cup} W_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \subset X\}_{i \in I}
              is locally finite, the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_x
              of indices
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in U_i
              is finite and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_x \subset K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,\leq)
              is a total order, it must contain an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒱
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J, \mathcal{V})
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_x \subset J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{V}
              is a cover and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              cannot belong to any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              outside of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_x
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %munder
                        %mo ∪
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi J
                            %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                      %mo ⊂
                      %munder
                        %mo ∪
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi J
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \underset{i \in J_x}{\cup} V_i \subset \underset{i \in J}{\cup} V_i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo ∪
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi I
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i \in I}{\cup} W_i
            %p
              This shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒲
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (K,\mathcal{W})
              is indeed an element of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T ,\leq )
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain"} chain
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\leq)
              has an upper bound, and so Zorn’s lemma implies the claim.
          %h2#references References
          %p The above account follows
